Subject: [PATCH 3/3] util: keep debug_dump_flags' buffers out of TLS

A dlopen()ed libGL cannot rely on glibc's static-TLS surplus: two 4 KiB
thread_local scratch buffers in debug_dump_flags() made PT_TLS 4400 bytes
against a 1664-byte surplus, and the first dlsym'd GL entry point that touched
the dispatch TLS then either failed to allocate ("cannot allocate memory in
static TLS block") or hung in the dynamic-TLS path.  They are debug-string
scratch buffers, not state: plain statics are correct and keep the DSO's TLS
under 100 bytes.

--- a/src/util/u_debug.c	2026-11-03 22:44:19.675325761 -0600
+++ b/src/util/u_debug.c	2026-11-03 22:44:19.675359073 -0600
@@ -408,8 +408,13 @@
 const char *
 debug_dump_flags(const struct debug_named_value *names, uint64_t value)
 {
-   static thread_local char output[4096];
-   static thread_local char rest[256];
+   /* HobbyOS/compat: NOT thread_local.  These are scratch buffers for a debug
+    * string, and as TLS they made this DSO's PT_TLS 4400 bytes -- far beyond
+    * glibc's 1664-byte static-TLS surplus for a dlopen()ed object.  A plain
+    * static keeps the whole DSO's TLS under 100 bytes, so a dlopened libGL
+    * needs no dynamic-TLS allocation at all. */
+   static char output[4096];
+   static char rest[256];
    int first = 1;
 
    output[0] = '\0';
